{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TNHW1z8oD9LUWoeq7PukDf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-521\"\n3\ttitle = \"The decomposition debt owner: four wide modules, M-06's four test monoliths, and no sensor watching the test tree\"\n4\tspecref = \"docs/plans/2026-08-25-remap-alignment.md\"\n5\tworkstream = \"process\"\n6\tsr_refs = []\n7\tneeds = []\n8\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n9\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n10\tpriority = 2\n11\t+++\n12\t\n13\t## Context\n14\t\n15\t**This row is the module-size ratchet's named DEBT OWNER.** The pointer in\n16\t`tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` moved here from `WI-508` in the same commit\n17\tthat filed this row, and the reason is the ratchet's own rule, applied one step\n18\tfurther than it has been before.\n19\t\n20\t### Why the pointer moved rather than waiting for `WI-508` to close\n21\t\n22\tThe ratchet's docstring records the chain: it directed active debt to `WI-280`\n23\tfor months after that item closed — \"a ratchet whose commentary names a closed\n24\titem tells the next author that the debt is somebody's when it is nobody's,\n25\twhich is the one thing a growth sensor must not do\" — so `WI-483` took ownership\n26\ton its first day, and handed it to `WI-508` at its close.\n27\t\n28\tTwo things make a third hand-off at close the wrong mechanism:\n29\t\n30\t1. **A close-time re-point is a promise; a filed row is a fact.** It has been\n31\t   honoured once, deliberately and with the defect named. Relying on it a second\n32\t   time makes the sensor's honesty depend on a future session remembering.\n33\t2. **`WI-508` was never the right owner for this AXIS, and the ratchet says so\n34\t   about its predecessor in the same words.** The docstring notes `WI-483`\n35\t   \"CLOSED having paid down the axis it was scoped for ... which is precisely\n36\t   NOT this file's axis\". The same is true here: `WI-508` is a **consolidation**\n37\t   program — minimize duplicated behaviour — while this ratchet measures module\n38\t   **size**, which is decomposition. `WI-508` inherited the pointer for being the\n39\t   live architectural program, not for being scoped to the axis.\n40\t\n41\tSo the pointer now names a row scoped to the axis it measures, and **`WI-508`'s\n42\teventual close has nothing to re-point.** That is the dead-owner defect made\n43\tunreachable rather than deferred again.\n44\t\n45\t**THIS ROW IS A STANDING DEBT OWNER, NOT A ONE-SITTING TASK.** Do not claim it\n46\texpecting to finish it. It is claimable for one scoped slice at a time, and it\n47\tis closed only when the debt below is paid or re-homed — and if it is ever\n48\tclosed, **the ratchet pointer must move in the same commit**, which is the rule\n49\tit inherited.\n50\t\n51\t### What it owns — 1: the four wide modules, corroborated from the requirements side\n52\t\n53\t`WI-508`'s blind derivation produced evidence this debt has never had. Two agents\n54\tderived a minimal module map from the requirements alone, and where **both**\n55\tagreed two obligations belong in *different* modules while the live tree fuses\n56\tthem, the fusion clusters hard:\n57\t\n58\t| live module | obligation pairs both derivations put APART |\n59\t| --- | --- |\n60\t| `agent_loop` | 14 |\n61\t| `check_trajectory` | 13 |\n62\t| `agent_common` | 10 |\n63\t| `bootstrap` | 5 |\n64\t| `trace`, `check_privacy` | 2 each |\n65\t| `check`, `check_doc_refs` | 1 each |\n66\t\n67\tfig: derived=\"pairs (x,y) of SRs where derivation A and derivation B each place x and y in different modules while the live SR->module join puts them in the same one; the live join reads LLR `module` cells through `sr_refs`\"\n68\t\n69\tThese are the same four modules the ratchet has baselined as its largest, reached\n70\tby a completely independent route — from what the requirements say belongs\n71\tapart, not from line counts. **That agreement is the row's strongest asset**: a\n72\tsize ratchet alone can be answered with \"it is big because it does a lot\"; this\n73\tsays which obligations a reader has to hold at once to read it.\n74\t\n75\t**It is NOT a mandate to split all four.** `WI-483` measured `check.steps` and\n76\tdeliberately LEFT it on four recorded grounds, and that decision stands. Any\n77\tslice here re-measures first and may reach the same answer.\n78\t\n79\t### What it owns — 2: M-06's four test monoliths, which now ride nothing\n80\t\n81\tRe-measured at the `WI-483` close: `tests/test_integrate.py` **3,520**,\n82\t`tests/test_trace.py` **2,099**, `tests/test_trajectory_arch.py` **1,927**,\n83\t`tests/test_agent_loop.py` **1,640**.\n84\t\n85\t`WI-483`'s item 4 ruled that a test split **rides along** with a subsystem\n86\tdecomposition and that a standalone split slice was out of scope. That rule was\n87\thonoured for all seven of its slices and it delivered nothing: every slice\n88\tchecked its touched tests and none needed a split. `WI-508` then filed no\n89\tsubsystem decomposition at all, so there was no vehicle to ride.\n90\t\n91\t**This row inherits them, and is explicitly NOT bound by that rule.** The\n92\tride-along constraint was `WI-483`'s own scope decision, not a standing ruling,\n93\tand it has now failed to deliver across two programs — which is the evidence\n94\tthat a rider with no vehicle is a rider that never moves. A standalone split is\n95\tin scope here. It should still be taken by stable behaviour boundary rather than\n96\tby line count, and a slice that decomposes a subsystem should still take its\n97\ttests with it.\n98\t\n99\t### What it owns — 3: the sensor gap, and the unruled question under it\n100\t\n101\t`tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` censuses `SCRIPTS` only, so **no armed\n102\tsensor watches the test tree** — which is why three of the four monoliths grew\n103\t5–36% between the 2026-08-19 review and the `WI-483` close with nothing saying\n104\tso.\n105\t\n106\t**Do not just extend the census.** That file's own docstring banks an unruled\n107\towner question — whether the line-count axis survives at all, given the owner's\n108\t`OI-16` correction that \"the monolith risk was always about FUNCTION size and\n109\tcomplexity, not file length\" and the worked counterexample where a structurally\n110\tsimpler `bootstrap.py` was made to demand a reviewed bump. Extending a disputed\n111\taxis to a second tree doubles whatever is wrong with it. The honest sequence is\n112\tto raise the axis question with the measurement this row can now supply, and\n113\textend only what survives the answer.\n114\t\n115\t### Standing constraints\n116\t\n117\t- Every slice ends green at the commit bar; a baseline is re-stamped only\n118\t  deliberately, with the reason in the log, and **never to clear a finding**.\n119\t- Moving lines into a new module is the intended escape hatch: the new module\n120\t  stays under `THRESHOLD` or earns its own reviewed baseline, and the shrunk one\n121\t  re-stamps downward in the same commit.\n122\t- If this row closes, **move the ratchet pointer in the same commit.**\n123\t\n124\t### SLICE 1 LANDED 2026-08-25 — the acceptance record leaves the checker\n125\t\n126\t**The evidence was RE-DERIVED before anything was designed, and it does not say\n127\twhat this row's table says.** The three-way agreement reproduces EXACTLY —\n128\tA vs LIVE **94.6%**, B vs LIVE **94.8%**, A vs B **97.0%** over the same 71 SRs\n129\tand 2,485 pairs — which is the strongest possible check that the re-derivation\n130\treads the same partitions the alignment pass read. The FUSION table does not\n131\treproduce:\n132\t\n133\t| live module | recorded (WI-508) | re-derived | tie-break stable? |\n134\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n135\t| `check_trajectory` | 13 | **13** | YES |\n136\t| `agent_loop` | 14 | **11** | no — rests on ONE tied SR |\n137\t| `agent_common` | 10 | 10 | YES |\n138\t| `bootstrap` | 5 | 5 | YES |\n139\t| `trace` / `check_privacy` | 2 / 2 | 2 / 2 | YES |\n140\t| `check` / `check_doc_refs` | 1 / 1 | 2 / 0 | no — one SR swaps |\n141\t| **total** | **48** | **45** | |\n142\t\n143\tfig: derived=\"pairs (x,y) of SRs where derivation A and derivation B each place x and y in different modules while the live SR->module join puts them in the same one; A and B read from their own `## Forward: every SR to exactly one owning module` tables, the live join reads LLR `module` cells through `sr_refs` and assigns each SR the module its rows name most often\"\n144\t\n145\t**Why the difference, and why it matters more than the difference.** The live\n146\tjoin's rule — *the module an SR's own LLR rows name most often* — is\n147\t**underdetermined for 13 of the 71 SRs**, whose top module is a TIE. `SR-026` is\n148\ta three-way tie between `agent_session`, `agent_loop` and `dispatch`; break it\n149\ttoward `agent_loop` and that module reads 14 and heads the table, break it any\n150\tother way and it reads 11 and does not. **The head of this row's strongest asset\n151\tturns on one arbitrary tie-break**, and nothing recorded which way the original\n152\trun went. That is stated here rather than quietly corrected: the table is still\n153\tgood evidence about WHICH modules fuse obligations, and it is not reliable about\n154\ttheir exact order.\n155\t\n156\t**`check_trajectory` is the worst offender under BOTH tie-breaks, so the choice\n157\tneeded no argument.** It reads 13 either way; it was the largest of the four\n158\tfusion heads at **4,963 lines** (`agent_loop` 3,614, `bootstrap` 3,146,\n159\t`agent_common` 2,643); it holds the kit's two most complex checker functions\n160\t(`main` 24, `interface_findings` 20); and unlike `agent_loop` — which `WI-483`\n161\tdecomposed twice — nothing had ever come out of it.\n162\t\n163\t**The boundary, in one sentence.** Everything that compares **two git trees**\n164\tcell by cell to answer whether attested text has moved away from the copy\n165\trecording its acceptance moved to `project-trajectory/scripts/acceptance_record.py`;\n166\teverything that asks what the registries say **today** stayed. 677 lines moved\n167\tVERBATIM: the §A5.1 cell split (`SPINE_TRACED_CELLS`/`SPINE_APPROVED_CELLS`,\n168\t`spine_cell_class`, `traced_cells`), the comparison (`SPINE_CSVS`,\n169\t`_spine_rows_at`, `_spine_revs`, `split_changed_cells`,\n170\t`staged_spine_amendments`), the two staged warns, and the mirror invariant in\n171\tboth staged and committed form.\n172\t\n173\t**The seam was FOUND, not carved, and the census is the proof.** The moved\n174\tblock's only non-builtin dependencies in 4,963 lines of scope were\n175\t`spine_carrier` and one git primitive — no `argparse`, `csv`, `re`, `difflib`,\n176\t`configparser` or `pathlib`. `tests/test_acceptance_record.py` pins that as the\n177\tboundary rather than re-asserting rules already covered where they were.\n178\t\n179\t**Both derivations asked for this module by name.** Team A's `A2` and team B's\n180\t`M06` are both \"Acceptance Record\", and 8 of `check_trajectory`'s 13 fused pairs\n181\trun through `SR-178`/`SR-179` — the largest single fusion reduction available in\n182\tthe module. Mechanically it was already visible: `intake.py` imported a\n183\t4,963-line validator, and **all three of its executable uses were inside the\n184\tmoved block**, so re-pointing them deleted the `intake -> check_trajectory`\n185\timport edge outright.\n186\t\n187\t**Byte-identical, measured that way.** Nine driven CLI paths\n188\t(`check_trajectory` ×5 including `--staged` and a non-root `--root`, `trace\n189\t--strict`, three `intake` help surfaces, `baseline_snapshot --help`) and 56 API\n190\tprobes over the live repo, capture-diffed against a HEAD-rebuilt scripts tree\n191\tafter the harness self-diffed empty twice. **One intended difference and no\n192\tothers**: `intake.py --help` prints its own docstring, which now names\n193\t`acceptance_record.staged_spine_amendments`.\n194\t\n195\t**Ratchets: one re-stamped DOWN, one RE-KEYED, one reviewed bump.**\n196\t`check_trajectory.py` **4,963 → 4,327** (−636); `acceptance_record.py` is 758\n197\tlines, under `THRESHOLD`, so it opens no entry. The complexity entry for\n198\t`committed_snapshot_findings` (12) was RE-KEYED to the new file, not re-stamped —\n199\tthe function is byte-identical and this file keys on (path, name), so a move has\n200\tto be spelled or the census reports the same 12 twice. `bootstrap.py` +7, the\n201\tMAPPING row and its reason.\n202\t\n203\t**TOPOLOGY DECISION (recorded here because module moves touch the spine).**\n204\tThree LLR `Module` cells re-point and **no new spine row is minted** — the\n205\tinstruction this row inherited is that a module move re-points TRACED cells only\n206\t(the `WI-483` slice 2/3 precedent), and re-pointing already contains the new\n207\tmodule, so a mint would have added `Drafted` rows to the owner's approval surface\n208\tfor nothing. `LLR-158` and `LLR-202` name `acceptance_record.py` alone.\n209\t**`LLR-178` names BOTH**, on cause rather than symmetry: its attested rationale\n210\tsays the mirror invariant \"lives in `check_trajectory` rather than in\n211\t`baseline_snapshot` because the writer must not also be the judge of its own\n212\twrites\", and its detail says it \"joins the failure set at `check_trajectory`'s\n213\tmain aggregation\". Both stay literally true through the re-export and the\n214\taggregation, and rewriting an `Approved` cell to tidy a diff is not a session's\n215\tact. `IF-091` (owner `LLR-158`, consumer `scripts/intake`) follows its owner and\n216\tnow declares `acceptance_record -> intake`, which is the live edge —\n217\tverified through `check_trajectory --strict`, which reported the containment\n218\terror before the re-point and the seam error before `intake` was moved, and is\n219\tCLEAN after both.\n220\t\n221\t**One shared helper widened, because the cut needed it.**\n222\t`check_trajectory._git` was a FOURTH copy of `kitlib.git.git_out` that the\n223\tD-8/`OI-16` consolidation missed — the same body plus an optional `stdin`, which\n224\tis why it read as a different function. `stdin` is now a parameter on `git_out`\n225\tand both modules alias the one home (the `check.py` idiom). Recorded as a\n226\tconsolidation act inside a decomposition slice rather than left unsaid.\n227\t\n228\t**M-06 rides nothing here, and the reason is measured rather than inherited.**\n229\tThe moved tier's tests live in `tests/test_trajectory_staged.py` (1,301 lines)\n230\tand `tests/test_baseline_snapshot.py` (966) — neither is one of M-06's four\n231\tmonoliths, and both drive the tier through the CLI or the re-exported API, so\n232\tneither needed to move. The four monoliths are re-measured for the record:\n233\t`test_integrate.py` **3,520**, `test_trace.py` **2,099**,\n234\t`test_trajectory_arch.py` **1,993** (was 1,927 at the `WI-483` close — it has\n235\tgrown again, with nothing watching), `test_agent_loop.py` **1,640**.\n236\t\n237\tfig: cmd=\"python -c \\\"import pathlib; [print(len(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines()), p.name) for p in sorted(pathlib.Path('tests').rglob('*.py'))]\\\"\" rev=c3bc6e07\n238\t\n239\t**The sensor gap stays CARRIED, not executed**, per this row's own §3.\n240\t\n241\t**An accident, recorded because a session that hides one teaches nothing.** The\n242\tbyte-identical harness drove `intake.py census` as if it were a read. It is not:\n243\tit minted `WI-522`/`WI-523` and COMMITTED the whole working tree. Reset with\n244\t`git reset --mixed`, the two minted specs deleted, and `docs/id-watermark`,\n245\t`docs/stage`, `docs/status.md`, `PROJECT_STATE.html` and\n246\t`components.derived.toml` restored to `c3bc6e07`; the watermark reads `WI = 521`\n247\tagain and no id was spent. The harness now drives `--help` on the subcommands\n248\tinstead, with the reason written at the site.\n249\t\n250\t**STILL OWED BY THIS ROW after slice 1.** The three remaining fusion heads\n251\t(`agent_loop`, `agent_common`, `bootstrap`), the rest of `check_trajectory`\n252\t(4,327 lines, 5 fused pairs left, `main` still at complexity 24), M-06's four\n253\tmonoliths, and the sensor gap. **Nothing here closes the row.**\n254\t\n255\t**Deferred to the owner: nothing new.** `LLR-178`'s rationale now locates the\n256\tjudge one indirection away from where the code sits; the multi-module cell keeps\n257\tthe sentence true, so this is a finding, not a decision withheld.\n258\t\n259\t### SLICE 2 LANDED 2026-08-25 — M-06's largest monolith, split standalone\n260\t\n261\t**The rider finally has no vehicle to wait for, so it walked.** `WI-483`'s item 4\n262\theld that a test split RIDES ALONG with a subsystem decomposition; it was\n263\thonoured across seven slices and delivered nothing, `WI-508` filed no\n264\tdecomposition at all, and slice 1 above found the same thing a third time — the\n265\tacceptance record's tests live in `test_trajectory_staged.py` and\n266\t`test_baseline_snapshot.py`, neither a monolith, and neither needed to move.\n267\t**Three programs, zero deliveries.** This row is explicitly unbound from that\n268\trule, and slice 2 is the standalone split.\n269\t\n270\t**Re-measured, and the worst offender is unambiguous.** `test_integrate.py`\n271\t**3,520** lines / 131 tests; `test_trace.py` 2,099 / 88;\n272\t`test_trajectory_arch.py` 1,993 / 86; `test_agent_loop.py` 1,640 / 66. No tie to\n273\tbreak here.\n274\t\n275\t**The boundary is the file's OWN, not a line count.** It already carried seven\n276\tnumbered banner sections; the split follows them, which is why it moves no\n277\targument:\n278\t\n279\t| module | subject | lines | tests |\n280\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n281\t| `test_integrate.py` | the CLAIM rung and the refusals in front of it | 932 | 42 |\n282\t| `test_integrate_admission.py` | what the slot ADMITS — outcome, the R1 mint refusal, the verdict gate, the declared bar, the branch harness, the window audit | 726 | 32 |\n283\t| `test_integrate_station.py` | the station protocol — refresh, attestation, merge slot — and the real-bar e2e | 1,129 | 36 |\n284\t| `test_integrate_unload.py` | the §5.6 unload of the branch and its worktree | 526 | 21 |\n285\t| `integrate_fixtures.py` | the shared surface (never collected) | 374 | — |\n286\t\n287\tfig: cmd=\"python -c \\\"import pathlib; [print(len(pathlib.Path('tests',n).read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines()), n) for n in ('integrate_fixtures.py','test_integrate.py','test_integrate_admission.py','test_integrate_station.py','test_integrate_unload.py')]\\\"\" rev=9c9e1aa7\n288\t\n289\t**`tests/integrate_fixtures.py` follows `traj_fixtures.py`'s stated rule\n290\texactly** (WI-277, which split a 5,359-line test monolith the same way): what\n291\tlives there is what MORE THAN ONE split module uses, **measured** — the git\n292\tplumbing, the repo builders, the pinned commit stamps, and the two builders whose\n293\tcallers straddle a boundary (`scaffolded_closed_branch`, `_worktree_count`).\n294\tAnything one module uses moved WITH that module: `claim_dir`/`spec_move` to\n295\tclaim, `verdict_repo` to admission, `station_repo` to the station,\n296\t`residue_lane` to unload.\n297\t\n298\t**The proof is node-id set equality, not a green.** The collected node ids of the\n299\tfour new modules are **byte-identical as a set** to the monolith's at `9c9e1aa7`\n300\t(133 ids, `diff` empty), and both sides run **132 passed / 1 skipped** — the skip\n301\tis the POSIX-only backslash test on Windows. Nothing was renamed, dropped or\n302\tquietly merged.\n303\t\n304\t**+167 lines across the family** (3,520 → 3,687): four module docstrings that\n305\teach state their own subject, four import blocks, and the shared file's own\n306\theader. Nothing executable was added and nothing was deleted.\n307\t\n308\t**Two tests were RE-HOMED rather than left where the line numbers put them.**\n309\t`test_the_git_dependency_is_declared_for_this_module` asserts the module's env\n310\tgate would have skipped — it went to the claim module; and\n311\t`test_bar_step_count_is_by_distinct_name_not_by_echoed_line` is a pure unit test\n312\ton the bar's step count in the merge record, so it went to the station beside the\n313\tbar it measures.\n314\t\n315\t**The commit bar is unmoved, deliberately.** All three new modules join\n316\t`conftest.SLOW_MODULES` beside the one they came out of — same heavy class (real\n317\tgit repos, real worktrees, the real bar in the e2e) — so smoke membership reads\n318\t**1,369 before and after** and the total **3,073 before and after**. A split that\n319\tquietly added 90 heavy tests to the per-commit bar would have been a regression\n320\tdressed as tidying.\n321\t\n322\t**Spine: four `Evidence` cells re-pointed, TRACED only, no row minted.**\n323\t`TC-132` now names claim + admission + station (its `method` spans all three),\n324\t`TC-146` and `TC-148` follow their named tests to the station, `TC-145` stays on\n325\tthe claim module. `Evidence` is a TRACED cell, so no attested prose moved;\n326\t`check_trajectory --strict` clean, `integrity=0`, `trace.py` findings unchanged.\n327\t\n328\t**M-06 after this slice: one of four done.** `test_trace.py` (2,099),\n329\t`test_trajectory_arch.py` (1,993) and `test_agent_loop.py` (1,640) remain, and\n330\tthe sensor gap stays CARRIED — extending a disputed line-count axis to a second\n331\ttree still doubles whatever is wrong with it.\n332\t\n333\t**Deferred to the owner: nothing new.**\n334\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"885c7821-4c9e-43a5-ba1c-40701acf8d48","uuid":"2fb0ec10-7b06-4477-9191-cdb4e77f9268","timestamp":"2026-08-30T10:51:11.668Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-drive\\wi521-decomposition-debt-owner\\docs\\work\\active\\wi521-decomposition-debt-owner\\WI-521-decomposition-debt-owner.md","content":"+++\nid = \"WI-521\"\ntitle = \"The decomposition debt owner: four wide modules, M-06's four test monoliths, and no sensor watching the test tree\"\nspecref = \"docs/plans/2026-08-25-remap-alignment.md\"\nworkstream = \"process\"\nsr_refs = []\nneeds = []\nbuildtier = \"strong\"\nsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\npriority = 2\n+++\n\n## Context\n\n**This row is the module-size ratchet's named DEBT OWNER.** The pointer in\n`tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` moved here from `WI-508` in the same commit\nthat filed this row, and the reason is the ratchet's own rule, applied one step\nfurther than it has been before.\n\n### Why the pointer moved rather than waiting for `WI-508` to close\n\nThe ratchet's docstring records the chain: it directed active debt to `WI-280`\nfor months after that item closed — \"a ratchet whose commentary names a closed\nitem tells the next author that the debt is somebody's when it is nobody's,\nwhich is the one thing a growth sensor must not do\" — so `WI-483` took ownership\non its first day, and handed it to `WI-508` at its close.\n\nTwo things make a third hand-off at close the wrong mechanism:\n\n1. **A close-time re-point is a promise; a filed row is a fact.** It has been\n   honoured once, deliberately and with the defect named. Relying on it a second\n   time makes the sensor's honesty depend on a future session remembering.\n2. **`WI-508` was never the right owner for this AXIS, and the ratchet says so\n   about its predecessor in the same words.** The docstring notes `WI-483`\n   \"CLOSED having paid down the ax
[... byte cap hit — full stream in out/run-logs/ ...]
026-08-30 — WI-521 slice 3: M-06's second monolith split, `test_trace.py`'s IF-seam tier walks\n\n**Summary.** `tests/test_trace.py`'s IF-### interface-seam tier moved verbatim to\na new `tests/test_trace_interfaces.py` — the standing decomposition-debt owner's\nsecond M-06 delivery, and the first taken after OI-68's 2026-08-30 ruling\nre-homed the row's §3 sensor/axis question to `WI-537`/`WI-538`.\n\n**Why this target.** The three remaining M-06 monoliths were re-measured:\n`test_trace.py` **2,323** (grew from 2,099 at slice 2 — the sensor gap in\naction), `test_trajectory_arch.py` **2,290**, `test_agent_loop.py` **1,640**. The\ntop two are 33 lines apart — no line-count winner — so the row's own rule\n(\"split by stable behaviour boundary, not by line count\") decided it: `test_trace`\ncarries a genuinely self-contained subsystem, `trace.py`'s IF-### interface-seam\ntier (`process.md` §8), with its own carrier, closed vocabularies, reachability\nadvisory and nine dedicated helpers; `test_trajectory_arch`'s sections are\nheterogeneous rules with no comparable seam.\n\n**Deliverable.**\n- New `tests/test_trace_interfaces.py` (978 lines / 40 tests): the IF-### tier —\n  id integrity + owner-shape `--strict` findings, the warn-first IF+CMP schema\n  tier, the endpoint reachability advisory, the OI-67 owner/consumers reshape and\n  IF carriage, and the WI-065 seam-citation join (`Verifies` cell ↔\n  `interfaces.toml`). Moved verbatim as one contiguous banner block.\n- `tests/test_trace.py` shrinks 2,323 → 1,370 (52 tests): the SN→SR→LLR→TC spine.\n  The two-line `_report` reader moved with its cluster; its four remaining core\n  call sites were inlined to the family's own `report.md`-read idiom (the only\n  non-move edit — ruff rewrapped those four lines, the +6 over a pure removal).\n- `tests/conftest.py`: `test_trace_interfaces` joins `SLOW_MODULES` beside\n  `test_trace` (same heavy class — a real `trace.py` subprocess per test), so\n  smoke membership is unchanged.\n- `docs/test/test-cases.toml`: three `TC` `Evidence` cells re-pointed to the new\n  module for the tests that moved (`test_if_tier_integrity`,\n  `test_channel_refuses_an_unknown_value_as_a_warn`,\n  `test_missing_required_if_field_is_a_warn`); the sibling ids that stayed were\n  left. `Evidence` is a TRACED cell — no row minted, no attested prose moved.\n\n**The proof is node-id set equality.** The sorted collected node-id sets of the\ntwo modules are byte-identical as a set to the pre-split `test_trace.py` at\n`56e7e52b` (92 ids, `diff` empty). Both run 91 passed / 1 skipped (the skip is\nthe POSIX-only provenance test on Windows).\n\nfig: derived=\"the sorted collected node ids of tests/test_trace.py + tests/test_trace_interfaces.py, stripped to `::name`, diffed against tests/test_trace.py at 56e7e52b — empty diff, 92 ids each side; 52+40 by module\"\n\n**Deviations from spec.** None. The slice follows the row's §2 (standalone\nM-06 split, boundary-first) and the slice-2 precedent (verbatim move, node-id\nequality proof, SLOW_MODULES co-membership, TRACED-only Evidence re-point). §3's\nsensor gap is not touched — OI-68 re-homed it to `WI-538` (soft edge, IF-054),\nrecorded in the spec's slice-3 section.\n\n**Byte deltas on budgeted files:** none touched (no `AGENTS.template.md`,\n`PROCESS.md`, `PROCESS_OPTIONS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, or guard skill in the diff).\n\n**Commit bar (this branch, Git Bash on Windows):** `-m smoke` **1378 passed, 6\nskipped in 31.21 s**; `check_smoke_budget --mode enforce` **27.4 s vs 60 s →\nwithin**; `check_docs --root . --stale` **0 broken** (the two `interfaces.toml`\nstale hints are pre-existing, not in this diff). The two split modules alone:\n**91 passed, 1 skipped in 241.60 s**. `trace.py --strict` interface-findings=0 /\nintegrity=0; `check_trajectory --strict` clean, graph acyclic.\n\n**Full suite:** _pending — recorded in the final commit._\n\n**M-06 after this slice: two of four done** (`test_integrate`, slice 2;\n`test_trace`, here). `test_trajectory_arch.py` (2,290) and `test_agent_loop.py`\n(1,640) remain. This row stays open — it is a standing debt owner.\n\nDeferred open items: none — this slice defers nothing new (the §3 sensor/axis\nquestion was owner-ruled and re-homed, per the summary above).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":57,"oldLines":8,"newStart":57,"newLines":22,"lines":[" **91 passed, 1 skipped in 241.60 s**. `trace.py --strict` interface-findings=0 /"," integrity=0; `check_trajectory --strict` clean, graph acyclic."," ","-**Full suite:** _pending — recorded in the final commit._","+**Full suite** (`pytest -q -n auto`, Git Bash on Windows): **1 failed, 3107","+passed, 16 skipped in 618.70 s**. The single failure is","+`test_derive_stage.py::test_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current` — the","+expected work-branch generated-artifact staleness, NOT a defect: `docs/stage`'s","+fingerprint hashes `docs/test/test-cases.toml` bytes (a `kitlib.stage`","+DECLARED_INPUT), so this slice's Evidence re-point drifted the input hash.","+`derive_stage.py --check` confirms **every derived value is unchanged** (stage","+`DevStg-LLReqs`, all per-phase values identical) — only the input fingerprint","+moved. `docs/stage` is a generated artifact the trunk lane regenerates after","+each merge (§5.2), which is why the pre-commit hook SKIPS its freshness check on","+a work branch; it is not re-stamped here (editing a generated artifact on a work","+branch is forbidden and would only collide with the trunk lane's regen). The two","+split modules and everything else pass."," ","+fig: cmd=\"python -m pytest -q -n auto\" rev=c9203f47","+"," **M-06 after this slice: two of four done** (`test_integrate`, slice 2;"," `test_trace`, here). `test_trajectory_arch.py` (2,290) and `test_agent_loop.py`"," (1,640) remain. This row stays open — it is a standing debt owner."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
